<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
  <head>
    {% # Inlined CSS Variables %}
    {% render 'css-variables' %}

    {% comment %}
      Font preloading:
      1. Preconnect to font CDN for faster connection
      2. Preload only the critical font variant (base weight)
      3. Additional variants load on-demand via @font-face
    {% endcomment %}
    {% unless settings.type_primary_font.system? %}
      <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.shopifycdn.com" crossorigin>

      {% comment %} Preload the base font variant for initial page render {% endcomment %}
      {{ settings.type_primary_font | font_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}
    {% endunless %}

    {% comment %}
      Newsreader is the other half of the type, and it is the half that renders
      the largest text on the page: every `h1` is `font-serif`, and on a product
      page so is the price. That makes it the LCP font on most templates, but
      it's self-hosted, so nothing discovers it until the inlined `@font-face`
      block above has been parsed and the text it styles laid out. Preloading
      the roman latin cut starts that fetch in the same breath as the CSS.

      Only the one cut. The italic is used in a footer tagline, and latin-ext
      only by currency symbols outside the latin block — preloading either
      would download bytes most pages never paint.
    {% endcomment %}
    {{
      'newsreader-variable.woff2'
      | asset_url
      | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous'
    }}

    {% # Load and preload the critical CSS %}
    {{ 'critical.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}

    {% # Tailwind utilities, compiled by Vite from src/styles/tailwind.css %}
    {{ 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

    {% # Global theme JS, compiled by Vite from src/main.js %}
    <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>

    {% # Social, title, etc. %}
    {% render 'meta-tags' %}

    {% # Browser tab, bookmark and home-screen icons %}
    {% render 'favicon' %}

    {{ content_for_header }}
  </head>

  <body>
    {% # First thing in the tab order on every page, so a keyboard or screen
       # reader shopper can get past the logo, the catalog row, search, account
       # and cart in one press. Off screen until it takes focus. %}
    <a class="skip-to-content" href="#main-content">
      {{- 'general.accessibility.skip_to_content' | t -}}
    </a>

    {% sections 'header-group' %}

    {% # The template's sections live in a landmark of their own, which is also
       # what `critical.css` grows to keep a short page's footer at the bottom.
       #
       # `tabindex="-1"` is what makes the skip link actually move focus rather
       # than only scroll: a landmark isn't focusable on its own. %}
    <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    </main>

    {% sections 'footer-group' %}
  </body>
</html>
